\[a_1 = 1 + \left(\frac{1}{2} - 1\right)^2 = 1 + \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)^2 = \frac{5}{4}.\]So $a_0 a_1 = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{5}{4} = \frac{5}{8}.$ Now,
\[a_2 = 1 + \left(\frac{5}{4} - 1\right)^2 = 1 + \left(\frac{1}{4}\right)^2 = \frac{17}{16}.\]So the product of the first three terms is $\frac{5}{8} \cdot \frac{17}{16} = \frac{85}{128}.$ Now,
